      "message": "txrequest: forget announcements by type, keep orphan parent requests\n\nA reconsiderable rejection of a witnessless copy of a transaction forgot its\nwtxid in TxRequestTracker regardless of announcement type, and since that\nwtxid equals the txid, it also cancelled every peer's txid-typed request for\nthe transaction, including orphan resolution requests for a missing parent.\nNow only wtxid-typed announcements of that hash are forgotten, so witnessless\nparents are treated like witnessed ones, which were never affected since\ntheir wtxid differs from the txid.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-12T21:12:10Z"
      },
      "author": {
