        }
      ],
      "message": "p2p: request an orphan's parents again when its retry still misses them\n\nWhen an orphan's parent is accepted, every request for it is forgotten\nand the orphan is queued for a retry. If the parent leaves the mempool\nbefore the retry, the retry fails for missing inputs and nothing\nrequests the parent again, so the orphan waits until it expires.\nRegister the orphan's announcers again as candidates for its missing\nparents when a retry still misses inputs, and remove the hole from the\nliveness target.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-12T21:12:10Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-08T13:16:11Z"
      },
      "sha": "ae9cfeb03f72da36c63d7223069f74502282a880"
    },
