          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/ae9cfeb03f72da36c63d7223069f74502282a880"
        }
      ],
      "message": "p2p: never check rejections by txid\n\nOrphan handling and txid lookups read the recent rejects filter by txid,\nbut the filter is keyed by wtxid and a witnessless transaction's wtxid is\nits txid, so a rejected witness-stripped copy of any confirmed or mempool\ntransaction made every orphan spending it be dropped. Never read the\nreject filters by txid, and no longer write txids to them: the entry for\nTX_INPUTS_NOT_STANDARD has no reader left, and the limit of one\nlow-feerate parent per orphan, which only ever matched witnessless\nparents, goes with the read. This is the change of #33066.\n\nThe cost, raised by ajtowns there, is bandwidth for a node whose policy\nis stricter than its peers': a parent rejected for a reason that depends\non the txid alone, such as a nonstandard input type, is downloaded again\nonce per announcer of each of its children until the next block. Each\ncopy is dropped by wtxid before validation.\n\nThis closes the last known hole in the liveness target, so the list of\nholes and the switch they turned off are removed from it.\n\nCo-authored-by: glozow <gloriajzhao@gmail.com>",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-12T21:12:10Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-08T13:43:54Z"
      },
      "sha": "73ce30f5559c2753091284f6e3b926a0a319a0f7"
    },
