          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/73ce30f5559c2753091284f6e3b926a0a319a0f7"
        }
      ],
      "message": "p2p: remember nonstandard-input rejections by txid\n\nThe previous commit stopped reading rejections by txid, the right\ndefault: a wtxid entry says nothing about other witnesses. One verdict\nis a function of the txid alone and is only reached once the inputs\nwere found, so no copy of a known transaction can produce it:\nTX_INPUTS_NOT_STANDARD. Without a txid record of it, a node whose\npolicy is stricter than its peers' (an unupgraded node after a soft\nfork) fetches such a parent once per announcer of each of its children,\nholds every descendant in the orphanage until it expires, and repeats\nthis at every level of a chain, since a held segwit orphan is not\nrecognised by txid either. Children of a remembered txid are dropped\nand remembered too, so a whole subtree costs one download per member.\n\nKeep these txids in a small exact set, cleared on each tip change,\nrather than in the bloom filter: a false positive here would drop an\nhonest child by txid along with its descendants. The set is capped at\n10,000 entries; once full, further rejections are not remembered until\nthe next block, which costs bandwidth and nothing else. This is the\ncase ajtowns raised on #33066.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-12T21:12:10Z"
      },
      "author": {
