        }
      ],
      "message": "fuzz: let the liveness target's honest peer bump its child\n\nThe honest peer may now announce child versions that do not pay for the\npair before the one that does, each replacing the previous one as a\nwallet bumping the fee would, and answers requests for replaced versions\nwith notfound. Adversaries can use every version.\n\nThis reaches two holes that need a second child from the same honest\npeer. They are flagged, and the property is not checked when one opens:\n\n- A completed request for the parent by txid to the honest peer is kept\n  while another peer's announcement of the txid is open, and makes the\n  honest peer's registration for the bumped child's parent a no-op.\n- An older version held for the honest peer after the bumped one is its\n  newest orphan, and only the package with it is tried.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-12T21:12:10Z"
      },
      "author": {
